<title>GERMANY: Tietmeyer says dollar correction should end now.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer says dollar correction should end now.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel. and Bundesbank president Hans Tietmeyer on Saturday said the dollar's correction should be completed now, but that the G7 summit was unlikely to come up with a formal agreement on the U.S. currency.</p>
<p>Speaking at a breakfast briefing before meetings with the six other most industrialised member nations which are part of the G-7, Tietmeyer said: &quot;the dollar correction process ought to end about now.&quot;</p>
<p>At the same time Tietmeyer added, &quot;The mark remains a stable and therefore strong currency.&quot;</p>
</text>
